    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "47c8861f-1427-3cf6-a733-9e0293488309",
                "word": "iterate",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "baef587d-e593-3ddd-844b-6e98f12d87b2",
                        "entry_id": "47c8861f-1427-3cf6-a733-9e0293488309",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Said or done again; repeated."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "021b1994-ea8c-4bb3-ac39-f2b72a5f202e",
                                "sense_id": "baef587d-e593-3ddd-844b-6e98f12d87b2",
                                "text": "When our faith is otherwise well enough known, there needs no iterate confession, saith Baldwin, which if, as he saith, it be vain boasting rather than a Christian vertue in us to offer it, it can be no lesse than needlesse, imperious usurpation in them to call as to it."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bca48417-a14f-3277-ae80-88fc05cda4b5",
                        "entry_id": "47c8861f-1427-3cf6-a733-9e0293488309",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Iterated."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee194670-a1d3-446c-87a0-ddf72379d3f9",
                                "sense_id": "bca48417-a14f-3277-ae80-88fc05cda4b5",
                                "text": "Therfore I beseche you brethren doe not neglect this holsome & profitable sacrament, but diligently consyder what ayde and what grace is geuen vnto you in it, & if by your necgligence & fal ye haue lost that grace, for a great part: yet it may be recouered agayne, not by a newe Confirmation, which may not be iterate, but by your inward conuersion & faythfull penaunce, and after ye bee risen and haue recouered your strength agayne, than take better hede, and do not make heauye, nor dryue not a∣way the holy ghost from you, who flieth alwaies from fained ypocrisy & wil not dwel in that body that is subiect and seruaunt to synne"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
